    </div>
    <figure>{img_tag('att_bin', 'Average HSC GPA by attendance band. No monotonic improvement is visible.')}</figure>
    <div class="warning-box">
      <strong>Surprising Finding:</strong> Both study hours and attendance are essentially uncorrelated with HSC results in this sample. The attendance-performance correlation is {s['att_corr']:.3f}, and study-hours correlation is {s['study_corr']:.3f}. Possible explanations: (1) attendance data may reflect enrollment rather than meaningful participation; (2) study hours may be self-reported and noisy; (3) the sample lacks very low attenders or studiers, truncating the observable range.
    </div>
