    </div>
    <div class="two-col">
      <figure>{img_tag('heatmap', 'Heatmap: District × School Type. Darker green = higher average HSC GPA.')}</figure>
      <figure>{img_tag('heatmap_gender', 'Heatmap: District × Gender. No consistent gender gap is visible across districts.')}</figure>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-box">
      <strong>Regional Insight:</strong> The district spread is modest (≈0.3 GPA points from lowest to highest). Rangpur and Rajshahi sit at the lower end, while Dhaka and Sylhet lead. School-type differences are minimal (Cohen's d = {s['effects'][3]['cohens_d']:.3f}). Targeted district-level curriculum support and teacher training in under-performing regions may yield higher returns than broad school-type reforms.
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- GPA Progression Delta Deep Dive -->
  <section>
    <h2>📉 GPA Progression Delta Deep Dive</h2>
    <p>The delta (HSC Result − Previous GPA) tells us whether the education system is adding value or merely preserving prior achievement.</p>
    <div class="two-col">
      <figure>{img_tag('delta_dist', f'Distribution of individual deltas. Mean = {s["delta_mean"]:.3f}, Std = {s["delta_std"]:.3f}.')}</figure>
      <figure>{img_tag('delta_district', 'District-level average delta. Negative bars indicate districts where students decline on average.')}</figure>
    </div>
    <figure>{img_tag('delta_socio', 'Delta broken down by internet access, private tuition, and parent education.')}</figure>
    <div class="warning-box">
      <strong>System Effectiveness:</strong> The national average delta is {s['delta_mean']:+.3f} — essentially flat. Several districts (e.g., Rajshahi, Rangpur) show negative average deltas, meaning students perform worse at HSC than they did previously. This is a red flag for system effectiveness in those regions.
    </div>
    <div class="insight-box">
      <strong>Equity Angle:</strong> Students with internet access and private tuition show slightly positive deltas, while those without show negative or near-zero deltas. The gap is small but consistent, suggesting that digital and coaching resources may help sustain progression rather than boost absolute scores.
    </div>
  </section>

